(EUROPEAN MEDICINES AGENCY \(EMA\) - COMMITTEE ON HERBAL MEDICINAL PRODUCTS \(HMPC\)) Tj
T*
(DIRECTIVE 2004/24/EC ON TRADITIONAL HERBAL MEDICINAL PRODUCTS \(THMPD\)) Tj
T*
(JURISDICTION: EUROPEAN UNION / INTERNATIONAL REGIMES) Tj
T*
T*
(Three Regulatory Pathways for Herbal / Ayurvedic Formulations in the European) Tj
T*
(Union:) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Traditional Herbal Medicinal Product \(THMPD - Simplified Registration\):) Tj
T*
(- Applies to herbal medicines with long-standing safety and plausible efficacy.) Tj
T*
(- Crucial Requirement: The applicant must demonstrate at least 30 years of) Tj
T*
(continuous traditional medicinal use, of which AT LEAST 15 YEARS must be within) Tj
T*
(the European Community / European Union.) Tj
T*
(- Challenge for Indian Ayurveda: Classical Ayurvedic formulations with) Tj
T*
(thousands of years of use in India often fail the 15-year EU usage requirement) Tj
T*
(unless historical trade or EU clinical presence is documented.) Tj
T*
T*
(2. Well-Established Use \(WEU\):) Tj
T*
(- Full marketing authorization based on bibliographic scientific evidence.) Tj
T*
(- Requires recognized efficacy and acceptable level of safety demonstrated) Tj
T*
(through published scientific literature over at least 10 years within the EU.) Tj
T*
T*
(3. Food Supplements:) Tj
T*
(- Governed under Food Supplements Directive 2002/46/EC.) Tj
T*
(- Cannot make therapeutic claims; only EFSA-approved botanical health claims) Tj
T*
(allowed.) Tj
